*5(b) Write a shell script that takes file name as arguments and convert all of them to uppercase*

*Theory*
- tr command is used to translate lowercase characters into uppercase characters
- mv command is used to rename a file

*Algorithm*
- Start the shell script
- Accept the file name as a command line argument $1
- Check whether the given file exists using the -f option
- If the file exists, convert its name from lowercase to uppercase using tr command
- Rename the file using mv command
- Display a message that the file name has been changed to uppercase
- If the file does not exist, display an appropriate error message
- Stop

*Shell Script*
#!/bin/bash
if [ -f "$1" ]
then
  mv "$1" "$(echo "$1" | tr '[:lower:]' '[:upper:]')"
  echo "File Name changed to Upper Case"
else
  echo "$1 does not exist"
fi
*Result*
The shell script was successfully executed and the given file name was converted to uppercase.
